# ripgrep, built from pinned upstream source as a files-only image the runner
# image copies by digest, for the tools server's grep and glob
# (agentry-notes plans/ripgrep-search.md D1, D3, D9; agentry-dockerimages#81).
#
# Default features only: no PCRE2 (plan D9). The Dockerfile checks the binary
# is static and that no PCRE2 or network crate is linked in; re-check that at
# every tag bump, and that scripts/check.sh --ripgrep-image still passes.
UPSTREAM_REPO=https://github.com/BurntSushi/ripgrep
UPSTREAM_COMMIT=e89fff89ac9af12e8d4ce9d5fd07beb408ca730f
UPSTREAM_TAG=15.2.0
UPSTREAM_LICENSE="Unlicense OR MIT"
# Built natively per architecture (PLATFORM=linux/amd64, PLATFORM=linux/arm64)
# and joined into one tag by scripts/build.sh --merge; the ripgrep workflow
# does both, then signs the joined digest. The tag is the build date and the
# workflow's run number, passed as IMAGE_TAG, and the workflow refuses a tag
# that exists, so a rebuild is a new tag and a new digest, never an overwrite.
IMAGE_NAME=agentry-ripgrep
PLATFORMS=linux/amd64,linux/arm64
